--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
unexpected expression
dropped the body
--
N5008 [stmt.select.general]/4 + [conv.bool]: a condition that is a
declaration `if(T a = x)' / `while(T a = x)' tests the declared object
contextually converted to bool.  The C++ front end converted the object to
bool itself and then handed the statement to the C type checker, which
converts the condition again; for a floating-point object the first
conversion is an `ieee_float_notequal' the second pass does not accept
("unexpected expression: ieee_float_notequal") and the function was
rejected (libstdc++'s three-argument std::hypot, `if (_Tp __a = ...)',
round-162 audit).  Fixed in round 163: the declared variable is left to the
statement's own conversion.  Covers class (explicit operator bool), pointer,
float and int conditions in if and while.
